    "body": "A static build linked with `--gc-sections` can drop the precomputed tables and code a program never calls, and the README does not say how. This adds a section on it, with the functions that use each table, the options that set the table sizes and the advice against `-Os`. It addresses the last open item of #1065.\n\n`text` size in bytes of a program linked against the static library, built with the default modules and the section's flags ([programs and commands](https://gist.github.com/fametrano/acf804a84a3cbb72fa1ce88cef60e96c/fe07e64d00a22dd104b4b8406f69bbd4a5b909dc)):\n\n| program | without gc | with gc | tables kept with gc |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ECDSA signing, `secp256k1_context_create` | 1341897 | 126952 | `ecmult_gen` |\n| ECDSA verification, `secp256k1_context_static` | 1342105 | 1124953 | `ecmult` |\n| ECDSA verification, `secp256k1_context_create` | 1342081 | 1229593 | both |\n| ECDH, `secp256k1_context_static` | 1342001 | 70740 | neither |\n\nMeasured with `size` and `nm` (Debian, aarch64, GCC 14.2, GNU ld 2.44). With gc, the CMake command gives the same sizes as the Autotools one for signing, verification with the static context and ECDH.\n",
