      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "I pushed the rewrite. The README no longer gives sizes. It describes the functions by context and table, names the table size options and advises against `-Os`.\n\nTo your question: besides verification, the `ecmult` table is used by public key recovery, public key tweaking and some MuSig2 and Silent Payments functions.\n\nOne point differs from your list: `secp256k1_ecdh` works with `secp256k1_context_static` and uses neither table, because it relies on `secp256k1_ecmult_const_ge`. The last row of the table in the PR description measures this, and the documentation of `secp256k1_context_randomize` names ECDH as the exception to its rule of thumb. So the section lists ECDH among the functions that use no table. Tell me if you meant something else.\n",
